      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Looks like a slightly higher bias used for speed 1 than speed 2 \u0026 3 (the spreadsheet result doesn\u0027t seem to include all these results)? \n\nInitially, we tested the CL with the same bias threshold for speed 2 and speed 1. As we noticed visible artifacts in the `Netflix_PierSeaside_2048x1080_60fps_8bit_420` sequence, we decided to reduce the bias for speed 2 similar to speed 3. We have updated both the results in the spreadsheet.\n\n\u003e  Is the result shown here the average of shorts set and hdres set? Can you provide the result for each set?\n\nYes, the results shared above are the average across the test sets. The individual results for each test set are as follows:\n```\n                        Instruction Count                                                                 \n                           Reduction(%)                        BD-Rate Loss(%)                Time Reduction(%)\ncpu-used  Resolution    Encoder   Decoder    avg.psnr   ovr.psnr   ssim     vmaf    vmaf_neg   dav1d Decoder   \n   1    \t  608P       -2.100    1.841      0.1526     0.1241   0.0681  -0.0677    0.0118      2.065\n   1        HDRES2       -1.281    1.746      0.0850     0.0788   0.0384   0.0406    0.0320      1.995\n   1       Average       -1.728    1.797      0.1219     0.1035   0.0546  -0.0185    0.0210      2.033\n   \n   2          608P       -0.704    1.595      0.0109     0.0082  -0.0141   0.0007    0.0045      1.584\n   2        HDRES2       -0.798    1.133     -0.0457    -0.0611  -0.0708  -0.1260   -0.0874      1.296\n   2       Average       -0.747    1.385     -0.0148    -0.0233  -0.0399  -0.0569   -0.0373      1.453\n   \n   3          608P       -0.029    2.127      0.1316     0.1548   0.0544   0.0881    0.0775      2.110\n   3        HDRES2       -0.275    1.262      0.0837     0.1409   0.1249   0.0039    0.0114      1.358\n   3       Average       -0.141    1.733      0.1098     0.1485   0.0864   0.0498    0.0475      1.768\n```",
